## Description

The sample code shown on the [Bun.WebView reference page](https://bun.com/reference/bun/WebView) times out at two points due to changes in bun.sh's HTML structure.

## Environment

- Bun version: 1.3.12
- Platform: macOS

## Steps to Reproduce

Run the sample code as documented:

```ts
await using view = new Bun.WebView({ width: 800, height: 600 });
await view.navigate("https://bun.sh");

await view.click("a[href='/docs']");   // ← hangs here
await view.scroll(0, 400);
await view.scrollTo("#install");       // ← would hang here too

const title = await view.evaluate("document.title");
const png = await view.screenshot({ format: "jpeg", quality: 90 });
await Bun.write("page.jpg", png);
```

## Root Causes

**1. `view.click("a[href='/docs']")` times out**

`click()` waits for actionability (element must be visible in the viewport).
On the current bun.sh, `a[href='/docs']` only exists in the "Learn more" card section and the footer — both below the fold at 800×600. The element never enters the viewport, so the actionability check never passes.

**2. `view.scrollTo("#install")` times out**

`id="install"` does not exist on bun.sh/docs. The installation section currently uses `id="/installation"`.

## Workaround

```ts
await using view = new Bun.WebView({ width: 800, height: 600 });
await view.navigate("https://bun.sh");

// Scroll element into viewport before clicking
await view.evaluate(
  `document.querySelector("a[href='/docs']").scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'instant', block: 'center' })`
);
await view.click("a[href='/docs']");

await view.scroll(0, 400);
await view.scrollTo('[id="/installation"]'); // correct selector for current bun.sh/docs

const title = await view.evaluate("document.title");
const png = await view.screenshot({ format: "jpeg", quality: 90 });
await Bun.write("page.jpg", png);
```

## Suggestion

Either update the sample code to use the workaround above, or consider pointing the sample at a more stable page whose structure won't change unexpectedly.

