Currently workers request permissions from a user. And it makes handling permissions against developer experience. It requires a developer to make evert single decision, when a software should do this for them. In my opinion workers should request permissions from their parent and the parent script should decide whether to ask user or to grant the permission on themselves

```ts
new Worker(new URL("worker.ts", import.meta.url), {
  deno: {
    async permissionsHandler(query: Deno.PermissionDescriptor)) {
       if (query.name === "read" && query.path.startsWith("tmp/")) {
         return {permissionResponse: "grant"}
       }
       return {permissionResponse: "deny"}
    }
  },
});
```

**Important**: The response should not be a true or false. It should be specific object to reduce errors

It could be `new Deno.PermissionsResponse("grant")` as a response

## Benefits

1. It would reduce the number of decisions to be made by user/developer. They do errors and could grant permissions just because they did it in the past without paying necessary attention
2. It would be easier to make trusted scripts to increase confidence in the workflows and tools

